      "writtenOn": "2022-08-25T19:39:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Interesting point. From what I can tell, IpClient always clears the addresses when entering StoppedState, so I think even if the addresses weren\u0027t cleared here, it should be okay, right?\n\nIn any case, I think this should be safe to merge. But I will leave a comment here to explain that this happens.\n\n---\nSo there are two situations:\na) new interface is discovered.\nb) running interface is discovered (e.g. an interface that moves from server back to client mode, ethernet is re-enabled, etc.).\n\nFor a): since the interface is not up, nothing has ever configured it. So I think setInterfaceUp() will essentially clear the address twice. This code path stayed the same.\n\nFor b): the address stays untouched. I think that\u0027s pretty much what setInterfaceUp() is trying to do anyways? IpClient will reset the addresses in its StoppedState#enter.",
